      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release, so this is about twice the limit. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\n1700 mg may be a typo, since 850 mg is a common tablet strength. Here are some options within the label:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals, then titrate.** This is a typical starting regimen if the patient is new to metformin.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the intended dose, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
