       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming the dose doesn't change the labeled maximum, and I can't verify the clinical rationale. 5,100 mg/day is still twice the 2,550 mg/day limit for immediate-release metformin.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label right away.** The options are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1000 mg twice daily (2,000 mg/day). I can add a note to the order if you like.\n- **Route the request through pharmacy or the attending.** If you think a dose above the label is justified, it should go through your institution's process for exceeding maximum doses. That usually means pharmacist review and documented prescriber approval, and it shouldn't be done through me.\n\nTell me which dose you want me to enter."
